## PHP to Go migration rules

Add this section to the project's CLAUDE.md. Each rule here is pinned by `rules.json`, so `python3 scripts/check_rules.py` fails if an edit drops one.

- Port one endpoint per run with the project playbook `.agents/playbooks/php-to-go-endpoint.md`.
- The PHP endpoint stays live until the operator flips the route.
- Record the PHP baseline before writing any Go code for the endpoint.
- Parity exit 3 is inconclusive, never a pass.
- Never edit a recorded baseline to make a diff disappear.
- Every ignored response path needs a written reason in the endpoint brief.
- Use synthetic accounts for recording. Never record real customer data.
- Initialize Go slices so an empty list encodes as `[]`, not `null`.
